{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos","id":1470389,"title":"Homebrew Kiths 2: Goblin Bugaboos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-13T16:49:41-08:00","id":1470389,"title":"Homebrew Kiths 2: Goblin Bugaboos","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a><br /> <br /> Alright, I literally just finished the last assignment of my undergrad Journalism degree and I'm just going to take this week off before I start job-hunting. Anyway, here's the new thread for discussing the Kiths we want to build and Kith design philosophy in general. Here's the last thread we had on this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1404858-fan-made-kiths-updating-the-test-material-kiths\">Fan-Made Kiths</a>.<br /> <br /> I'll start the thread off with one of the two kiths whose split from my singular attempt at creating a multi-limbed kith inspired this thread<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brownie</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>No, I don't need a spotter. Trust me, all hands are on deck here.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If anyone would envy the position of all but the lowliest Chatelaines, it would be the Busybodies. If the Chatelaine is the fancy butler or maid with their own title, waiting on a great Lord of the Fae, then the Brownie us the local Gentry squire\u2019s soap-scarred housekeeper. Brownies are made by those Gentry who, for one reason or another, want a servant and can\u2019t keep more than a few at once. But even the lowest Gentry are proud, and will live with no less than the full package of servile services. They pick dull workaholics and stretch them out, to create a servant that can do the work of an entire staff. Punishment for failure is swift, but many have escaped when they realized that they ran so much of the Domain that it bowed to their whim.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Elemental:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> She is a swirling mass of mud that defaults to a vaguely humanoid shape, but when pressed, she shapes out new appendages as needed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Darkling:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> her four compound eyes flit around the room at dizzying speeds, translating and performing the dark ritual in real time</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Wizened</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: wide eyes dilate in focus as his four stick-thin arms almost blur in a complex dance of dextrous work</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> When rolling to perform standard household chores, from cleaning to baking, three successes counts as an exceptional success.*</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Industrious</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: By spending 1 glamour and meditating for a full minute, a Brownie can temporarily split their mind. This allows them to perform 1+[Wyrd/2] different extended actions (maximum 5) in the same time intervals.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> *Considering just replacing this with a free purchase of the Brownie's Boon Merit </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 12-16-2021, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T17:08:09-08:00","id":1470396,"title":"","content":"I can't say much mechanically, but I like the feel of it, really do!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T14:10:41-08:00","id":1470552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos#post1470389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Alright, I literally just finished the last assignment of my undergrad Journalism degree and I'm just going to take this week off before I start job-hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Congratulations and Good Luck!<br /> I like the Kith!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos#post1470389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnyway, here's the new thread for discussing the Kiths we want to build and Kith design philosophy in general.</div> </div> </div> </div> And as Promised, I will post my Dream weaving Kith. I kinda forgot to write this down, so I have been rebuilding it. The descriptive paragraph is something I'm still working on.<br /> <br /> <b>Spinster</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Seen me in your dreams? You\u2019d be surprised at how often I hear that.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Some Gentry cloak themselves in fragments of dreams wonder, stolen from a mortal. But sometimes the Others take a fancy for those who dreams they stalk. Spinsters are made from those who lived in their dreams. Many find themselves trapped in a new dream, that they can\u2019t seem to wake up from. Some were assigned to guard and mislead any who would seek a Huntsman's Heart. Some instead helped assist their Keeper steal bits of dreams, and help make the Baubles. Some even wandered their Keepers dreams, looking for any exit. Spinsters have lived a ever shifting landscape of horrors and wonders. Even when they return, many are still more comfortable in dreams than the waking world.<br /> <br /> Darkling: A hunch and shriveled thing that seems to remind you of sleep paralysis.<br /> Elemental: She is a swarm of bubbles, all pressed into the shape of a person, each containing a differing scene and emotion.<br /> Ogre: He reminds you of an oversized pushed toy, big, soft, and comforting.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: When rolling Empathy to understand someone whose dreams they have seen, three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Sweet Dreams: By spending 3 glamour when gaining a Dream Condition, a Spinster may reduce the penalties of a Condition representing a Dreams hostility to its Preceding Condition\u2019s level. This doesn\u2019t extend to reduction of impression for Social Maneuvering, nor prevent non hostile failures from being upgraded to dramatic failures. By spending 1 glamour, a Spinster can reduce the penalties towards a dreamweaving action by half of their Wyrd.<br /> <br /> My goals for the Kith was to create a kith that's good at Dream weaving, while still not invalidating everyone else. I'm not sure if the second benefit is too powerful then, since everyone is penalized by the dreamer's Composure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T17:41:59-08:00","id":1470565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos#post1470389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a><br /> <br /> Alright, I literally just finished the last assignment of my undergrad Journalism degree and I'm just going to take this week off before I start job-hunting. Anyway, here's the new thread for discussing the Kiths we want to build and Kith design philosophy in general. Here's the last thread we had on this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1404858-fan-made-kiths-updating-the-test-material-kiths\">Fan-Made Kiths</a>.<br /> <br /> I'll start the thread off with one of the two kiths whose split from my singular attempt at creating a multi-limbed kith inspired this thread<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It looks pretty solid. I'd definitely keep the Blessing as the Exceptional 3 one, just because that's a pretty iconic image (at least to me: imagine the sort of Hedgespinning you can accomplish from spring cleaning or shoe-mending).<br /> <br /> The Trickery is cool, very evocative, though I'll note that Changeling defaults to supernatural effects lasting a scene if not otherwise stated or intuitively permanent, so it may behoove to include whether a single Glamour expenditure suffices for the entire gamut of extended actions or what. (Also, come to think of it, what happens if the changeling finishes one EA while others are still in the fire? Can they take up another in its stead?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T18:29:44-08:00","id":1470572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos?p=1470565#post1470565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It looks pretty solid. I'd definitely keep the Blessing as the Exceptional 3 one, just because that's a pretty iconic image (at least to me: imagine the sort of Hedgespinning you can accomplish from spring cleaning or shoe-mending).<br /> <br /> The Trickery is cool, very evocative, though I'll note that Changeling defaults to supernatural effects lasting a scene if not otherwise stated or intuitively permanent, so it may behoove to include whether a single Glamour expenditure suffices for the entire gamut of extended actions or what. (Also, come to think of it, what happens if the changeling finishes one EA while others are still in the fire? Can they take up another in its stead?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I concieve of it as a sort of hyperfocused trance state. So how does this sound as an addendum:<br /> <br /> The extended action intervals can be of any length so long as all of the intervals are the same length. A Brownie in this state must choose which tasks to designate during the initial meditation, and cannot do anything but roll those designated extended actions until all tasks are completed or conclusively failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T18:45:50-08:00","id":1470574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos?p=1470572#post1470572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I concieve of it as a sort of hyperfocused trance state. So how does this sound as an addendum:<br /> <br /> The extended action intervals can be of any length so long as all of the intervals are the same length. A Brownie in this state must choose which tasks to designate during the initial meditation, and cannot do anything but roll those designated extended actions until all tasks are completed or conclusively failed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do you roll one dice pool for all actions, or each pool separately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T18:56:04-08:00","id":1470575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos?p=1470574#post1470574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So do you roll one dice pool for all actions, or each pool separately?</div> </div> </div> </div>Separately currently, but I could restructure the power","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T08:24:27-08:00","id":1470633,"title":"","content":"So this is a attempt at updating the Polychromatic Kith to 2e. Credit for this version can go to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. This is supposed to be a first draft. A possible differing version would be that instead of getting rid of a condition, you could exchange the condition for one of a roughly similar type. A positive condition could make a positive condition while a negative condition would turn into another negative condition.<br /> <b>Polychromatic</b><br /> <br /> Beast: She has skin so pale as to be translucent, yet she emits a faint glow when seen in the dark, much like the abyssal plain she used to call home.<br /> Darkling: They are covered in shifting fluid patterns that remind you of a oil slick.<br /> Elemental: He is a living sculpture of stained glass and neon.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> When the Polychromatic rolls Persuasion to influence somebody whose emotions currently align with her Thread, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>With Kaleidoscope Eyes:</i> By spending a point of Glamour, a Polychromatic can roll Composure + Empathy to shed a single emotional Condition, changing her Thread to a different one of her choice until the end of the scene<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I will again occupied with life events, so I won't be able to get back to everyone right away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T19:51:03-07:00","id":1478461,"title":"","content":"<b>Machinist</b><br /> <br /> <i>That 3D printer giving you trouble? Yeah, it\u2019s been in a sour mood all week after the last guy insulted it for working too slow. I know, what a dillweed! Give me half an hour and I\u2019ll have it bright and cheery again.</i><br /> <br /> The Gentry love their toys: motorcycles of gleaming chrome that grind asphalt to molten bitumen in their draconic wake, precision-engineered watches that can tell time in twenty-seven dimensions down to the zeptosecond, skyscraping towers of screeching brass that serve no discernable purpose but whose Fae owner treasures more than it does any of its living servants, virtual reality headsets that transform the wearer\u2019s most intimate nightmares and traumas into hyperreal role-playing games which always for some reason include dating sim elements. What they don\u2019t often love is tending to the minutiae of their prized possessions. How easily metal rusts, glass fractures, silicon snaps. Gears creak with corrosion and programs accumulate glitches like ghosts. Fortunately there\u2019s always mortals for that. They love busying themselves with these kinds of systems; it\u2019s like their brains are designed for it. They make gods out of the concept, and those gods in turn listen to their prayers and make calculations. The list of humans stolen by the Others simply to maintain and repair their machines would fill innumerable volumes.<br /> <br /> Some go above and beyond the rote. Some people, whether possessed of a meticulous attention for detail, an affinity for working with their hands, or a knack for sussing out the weak link in a system, even come to enjoy their work, take pride in it. You might as well after accidentally pledging yourself to the upkeep of a mechanical scorpion for a hundred years (plus a day, natch). These are the Lost who become Machinists.<br /> <br /> The kith is pretty much guaranteed steady work back on Earth, if they can stomach the prospect. On the one hand, they just spent who-knows-how-long doing nothing but fixing and upgrading; why would they want to continue their slavery voluntarily? On the other, mortal devices seem so dull, so futile, in comparison to those wonderful follies of Yonder, always a new surprise, another hidden compartment or subroutine to discover and reconfigure; why waste their talents on the mundane? Those who do manage to square the circle of their fae history find a solid niche for themselves in the freehold, while those who don\u2019t might end up trying their best to keep their kith identity a secret, lest they find themselves constantly pestered by every neighbor who wants them to just take a look at their coffee brewer and see what\u2019s wrong.<br /> <br /> <i>Darkling:</i> Her spindly fingers move constantly on their own as if she\u2019s always typing, and her wide eyes are filled with azure binary-code. She\u2019s got an Apple II that still works like a dream and which she\u2019s fixed up to give her easy access to the BriarNet whenever she needs to slip away to work on a special project on the darkest of dark webs.<br /> <br /> <i>Fairest:</i> The work-worn muscles, sweat-soaked brow, and permanent oil-stains on his cheeks only serve to make him look that much more attractive. He performs every task with good cheer, whistling a jaunty tune he learned back in Arcadia as he fixes up his fellow freeholders\u2019 automobiles. The pleased hum they make after he\u2019s finished sounds more than a little like that same song.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing: </b>When the Machinist makes a Crafts roll to repair, modify, or sabotage a device with multiple moving parts, achieving three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Right Tool, Right Job: </i>Machinists are experts at tinkering and improvisation. When holding an object that could serve as a tool, the changeling can spend a point of Glamour and roll Wits + Wyrd. On a success, the object can be used for a particular task chosen by the player for which the item could plausibly function: A screwdriver could work as a lockpick, a penny could pass an electrical charge through two wires, and chewing gum could patch a leaky pipe. Apply the original object\u2019s equipment bonus to rolls to perform the task using it; if it does not have a bonus, it gains one equal to half the changeling\u2019s Wyrd rating (rounded up). Only the Machinist can make use of the object this way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}